% Surveys of the Philadelphia Contributionship, 1752-1810, judged by the
% rules of contributionship.le in force in the year each was made, and
% compared with what the Board did.
%
% The sample (scenario "sample") is every survey of the Contributionship
% for which a typed source gives a year, collected on 24 September 2026: a
% transcription of the survey itself, a National Park Service historic
% structure report that summarises it, a journal article, or the
% catalogue record of the Contributionship's digital archive (policy
% number, year, amount). The comment above each survey's facts gives its
% number, date, owner and building, and the kind of evidence. A survey
% states only what its source states: most give the building and its
% stories, few give the walls, the roof or the rate.
%
% The sample is not random: it leans to brick houses around Independence
% Mall and to famous buildings, and every survey in it was insured. No
% refusal is recorded in any typed source; the Board minutes, where
% refusals were written, survive only as scanned handwriting. The other
% scenarios are invented houses that the rules would refuse, one per rule.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the historical records it cites,
% and it is not legal or insurance advice. Its authors accept no liability
% for any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base contributionship surveys includes these resources:
    contributionship.

the knowledge base contributionship surveys includes:


the Papers of Benjamin Franklin is published at "https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Franklin/01-13-02-0126".
the NPS Independence Mall study block one is published at "https://npshistory.com/publications/inde/hrs-mall-block-one.pdf".
the NPS Independence Mall study block two is published at "https://npshistory.com/publications/inde/hrs-mall-block-two.pdf".
the NPS Independence Mall study block three is published at "https://npshistory.com/publications/inde/hrs-mall-block-three.pdf".
the NPS City Tavern report is published at "https://npshistory.com/publications/inde/hsr-ads-city-tavern.pdf".
the NPS Franklin House report is published at "https://npshistory.com/publications/inde/hsr-franklins-house.pdf".
the NPS Todd House grounds report is published at "https://pubs.nps.gov/eTIC/HOSP-INDU/INDE_391_134872_0001_of_0088.pdf".
the NPS report INDE 134861 is published at "https://pubs.nps.gov/eTIC/HOSP-INDU/INDE_391_134861_0001_of_0036.pdf".
the NPS Bishop White House report is published at "https://npshistory.com/publications/inde/fp-bishop-white-house-v1.pdf".
the Contributionship archive catalogue is published at "https://www.philadelphiabuildings.org/contributionship/search.cfm".
Lawler 2002 is published at "https://journals.psu.edu/pmhb/article/view/45510".

query refused is:
    which survey is refused under which rule.

query special is:
    which survey needs a special agreement under which rule.

query departures is:
    which survey departs from the rules under which rule.

query above table is:
    the deposit of which survey exceeds the table by which number shillings.

query insured is:
    the Board insured which survey.

query table is:
    the table deposit for which survey is which number shillings.

query additional is:
    which survey needs an additional deposit under which rule.

query conflicts is:
    the decision on which case about which issue conflicts with which second case.

