% Invented: a wooden house surveyed in 1772, after the ban of April 1769.
scenario wooden_house_1772 is:
    the Vine Street house was made in 1772.
    the building of the Vine Street house is built of wood.
    refused expects answers ["the Vine Street house is refused under the ban on wooden buildings"].

% Invented: a wooden house surveyed in 1760, before the ban: insurable only by
% special agreement with the Directors (Article 7).
scenario wooden_house_1760 is:
    the Vine Street house was made in 1760.
    the building of the Vine Street house is built of wood.
    refused expects answers [].
    special expects answers ["the Vine Street house needs a special agreement under the wooden houses article"].

% Invented: a brick house with a tree before it in the street, 1790.
scenario street_tree_1790 is:
    the Arch Street house was made in 1790.
    the party walls of the Arch Street house are 9 inches thick.
    the Arch Street house records a tree before the house in the street.
    refused expects answers ["the Arch Street house is refused under the ban on trees"].

% Invented: the same house in 1815: insurable, with an additional deposit
% (revision of 1810).
scenario street_tree_1815 is:
    the Arch Street house was made in 1815.
    the party walls of the Arch Street house are 9 inches thick.
    the Arch Street house records a tree before the house in the street.
    refused expects answers [].
    additional expects answers ["the Arch Street house needs an additional deposit under the revision of 1810"].

% Invented: the same house in 1825: no additional deposit since 1823.
scenario street_tree_1825 is:
    the Arch Street house was made in 1825.
    the party walls of the Arch Street house are 9 inches thick.
    the Arch Street house records a tree before the house in the street.
    refused expects answers [].
    additional expects answers [].

% Invented: a house twelve miles from Philadelphia, 1760 (Article 3).
scenario twelve_miles_1760 is:
    the Chester road house was made in 1760.
    the house of the Chester road house stands 12 miles from Philadelphia.
    refused expects answers ["the Chester road house is refused under the ten mile limit"].

% Invented: a house out of the city, 1770, with no iron rails and no trap door
% (the order of 12 April 1768).
scenario out_of_city_1770 is:
    the Germantown house was made in 1770.
    the house of the Germantown house is out of the city.
    the party walls of the Germantown house are 9 inches thick.
    refused expects answers ["the Germantown house is refused under the order of 1768"].

% Invented: the same house with iron rails and a way out onto the roof.
scenario out_of_city_1770_railed is:
    the Germantown house was made in 1770.
    the house of the Germantown house is out of the city.
    the Germantown house records iron rails on the roof.
    the Germantown house records a way out onto the roof.
    the party walls of the Germantown house are 9 inches thick.
    refused expects answers [].

% Invented: a house of the best class of the 1752 table: nine inch party walls
% carried above the roof, a door onto the roof, iron rails.
scenario first_class is:
    the Walnut Street house was made in 1755.
    the party walls of the Walnut Street house are 9 inches thick.
    the party walls of the Walnut Street house are carried above the roof.
    the Walnut Street house records a way out onto the roof.
    the Walnut Street house records iron rails on the roof.
    table expects answers ["the table deposit for the Walnut Street house is 15 shillings"].
